d><code>Vec&lt;ForceLink&gt;</code>: <code>{ source, target, weight }</code>, where <code>source</code> and <code>target</code> are indexes into <code>data</code></td><td>none</td></tr><tr><td><code>iterations</code></td><td><code>usize</code>: force steps</td><td><code>240</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>distance</code></td><td><code>f32</code>: preferred gap between linked circles, in pixels</td><td><code>14.</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>show_labels</code></td><td><code>bool</code>: names written inside circles that are big enough</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>legend</code></td><td><code>Legend</code>: one entry per group</td><td>shown</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Groups are laid out as a squarified treemap, so each cell&#39;s area follows its total value. Inside a cell, nodes are circles sized by their share of it. A force simulation pulls linked nodes together, keeps circles from overlapping and keeps each one inside its own cell. Links between cells are drawn across the borders, and the circles are pulled toward the cell they link to. Links with a missing index, or from a node to itself, are ignored. Hiding a group in the legend gives its space to the rest.</p>\n","examples":[{"id":"microservices","title":"Microservices","description":"Each team is a treemap cell sized by its nodes' values; calls are pulled across cells.","code":"<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">treemap!</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(microservices, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">services</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(), </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">service_links</span><span style